# Contributing to {{ project_name }}

Thanks for contributing!

## Setup

```bash
just install
```

## Before you open a PR

- `just qa` must pass (lint, type-check, tests).
- Add tests for new behavior (see `guidelines/testing.md`).
- Update `CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]`.
- Update docs where relevant (see `guidelines/documentation.md`).

Pre-commit runs automatically on every commit. Run all hooks manually with
`just lint`.

## Notes for editors

- `docs/skills/` is a **symlink** to the top-level `skills/` directory (set
  during `copier copy`). Don't delete or commit the resolved files — edit the
  originals under `skills/` and let MkDocs follow the link. If the symlink is
  ever lost, re-create it with `ln -s ../skills docs/skills` (Unix/WSL2 only).
- **Bumping ruff (or any tool with both a `pyproject.toml` pin and a
  `.pre-commit-config.yaml` `rev:`)** — touch both in the same commit so
  `just qa` and `pre-commit run --all-files` stay in lockstep (the quality
  gate must stay green). The fastest path is `uv lock --upgrade-package ruff`
  followed by `uv run pre-commit autoupdate --repo https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff-pre-commit`.
